<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Significance of Kasaragod</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Lora:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&family=Poppins:wght@300;400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
            /* Kerala inspired background pattern/color */
            background-color: #f4f1ea; 
            background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg width='60' height='60' viewBox='0 0 60 60' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cg fill='none' fill-rule='evenodd'%3E%3Cg fill='%23d6d0c4' fill-opacity='0.4'%3E%3Cpath d='M36 34v-4h-2v4h-4v2h4v4h2v-4h4v-2h-4zm0-30V0h-2v4h-4v2h4v4h2V6h4V4h-4zM6 34v-4H4v4H0v2h4v4h2v-4h4v-2H6zM6 4V0H4v4H0v2h4v4h2V6h4V4H6z'/%3E%3C/g%3E%3C/g%3E%3C/svg%3E");
        }
        h1, h2, h3, .serif-font {
            font-family: 'Lora', serif;
        }
        
        /* Modern Frame Scrollbar Styling */
        .frame-content::-webkit-scrollbar {
            width: 8px;
        }
        .frame-content::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
            background: #e5e7eb;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        .frame-content::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
            background-color: #065f46; /* Emerald 800 */
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        
        /* Subtle Kerala motif borders */
        .kerala-border {
            border: 4px solid #065f46;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 8px 10px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
            position: relative;
        }
        .kerala-border::before {
            content: '';
            position: absolute;
            top: 4px; left: 4px; right: 4px; bottom: 4px;
            border: 1px dashed #047857;
            border-radius: 8px;
            pointer-events: none;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body class="h-screen flex flex-col overflow-hidden text-gray-800">

    <header class="bg-emerald-900 text-white shadow-lg z-10 relative">
        <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-6 text-center">
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-wide text-amber-400">Discover Kasaragod</h1>
            <p class="mt-2 text-emerald-100 italic text-lg md:text-xl font-light">The Crown of Kerala & Sapthabhasha Sangamabhoomi</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Decorative bottom border -->
        <div class="h-1 w-full bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-600 via-amber-300 to-amber-600"></div>
    </header>

    <main class="flex-1 overflow-hidden p-4 md:p-6 lg:p-8">
        <!-- The Grid Container: Stacks on mobile (h-auto), 3 columns on desktop (h-full) -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 h-full pb-16 md:pb-0 overflow-y-auto md:overflow-hidden">
            
            <!-- FRAME 1: Tourist Attractions -->
            <section class="kerala-border bg-white h-[60vh] md:h-full flex flex-col">
                <div class="bg-emerald-100 p-4 rounded-t-lg border-b-2 border-emerald-800 text-center relative z-10">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-emerald-900">Tourist Attractions</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="frame-content flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-5 relative z-10 space-y-6">
                    <article>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-amber-700 mb-2">Bekal Fort</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            The largest fort in Kerala, Bekal Fort is a spectacular keyhole-shaped historical monument situated right by the Arabian Sea. It offers breathtaking views and a glimpse into the region's rich military past, standing strong for over 300 years.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                    <hr class="border-amber-100">
                    <article>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-amber-700 mb-2">Ranipuram</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            Often referred to as the "Ooty of Kerala," Ranipuram is a stunning hill station nestled in the Western Ghats. Its lush green shola woods, monsoon forests, and diverse wildlife make it a paradise for trekkers and nature lovers.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                    <hr class="border-amber-100">
                    <article>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-amber-700 mb-2">Ananthapura Lake Temple</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            The only lake temple in Kerala, believed to be the original seat (Moolasthanam) of Ananthapadmanabha Swami. The temple was historically guarded by a legendary, vegetarian crocodile named Babiya, adding to the mystical aura of the sacred shrine.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- FRAME 2: Cultural Heritage -->
            <section class="kerala-border bg-white h-[60vh] md:h-full flex flex-col">
                <div class="bg-amber-100 p-4 rounded-t-lg border-b-2 border-amber-800 text-center relative z-10">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-amber-900">Cultural Heritage</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="frame-content flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-5 relative z-10 space-y-6">
                    <article>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-emerald-700 mb-2">The Land of Seven Languages</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            Kasaragod is uniquely known as <em>'Sapthabhasha Sangamabhoomi'</em> (The land of seven languages). Due to its bordering geography, you can hear a harmonious blend of Malayalam, Tulu, Kannada, Marathi, Konkani, Beary, and Urdu here.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                    <hr class="border-emerald-100">
                    <article>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-emerald-700 mb-2">Theyyam Rituals</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            Theyyam is a vibrant and ancient ritualistic art form prominent in North Malabar. Performers don spectacular costumes and elaborate face painting, embodying divine deities. It bridges the gap between the divine and humanity through powerful dance.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                    <hr class="border-emerald-100">
                    <article>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-emerald-700 mb-2">Yakshagana</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            A traditional theater form that combines dance, music, dialogue, and extravagant costumes. Highly popular in the Tulu-speaking regions of Kasaragod, it narrates epic stories from the Ramayana, Mahabharata, and Puranas.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- FRAME 3: Handlooms & Geography -->
            <section class="kerala-border bg-white h-[60vh] md:h-full flex flex-col">
                <div class="bg-blue-100 p-4 rounded-t-lg border-b-2 border-blue-800 text-center relative z-10">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-blue-900">Handlooms & Geography</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="frame-content flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-5 relative z-10 space-y-6">
                    <article>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2">Kasaragod Saree</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            Holding a Geographical Indication (GI) tag, the Kasaragod Saree is a traditional cotton handloom renowned for its high quality, durable thread work, and distinct traditional borders. It is a testament to the local weavers' enduring craftsmanship.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                    <hr class="border-blue-100">
                    <article>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2">Pristine Coastlines & Rivers</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            The district is bordered by the majestic Western Ghats on the east and the Arabian Sea on the west. It is blessed with 12 rivers, including the Chandragiri and Tejaswini, weaving through lush landscapes, creating beautiful backwaters and golden beaches.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                    <hr class="border-blue-100">
                    <article>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2">Coir Industry</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            Abundant in coconut groves, Kasaragod sustains a thriving traditional coir industry. The golden fiber extracted from coconut husks is woven into mats, ropes, and crafts, supporting the livelihood of local rural communities.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </section>

        </div>
    </main>

</body>
</html>